{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7cbfb5d7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002387,"end_time":"2026-11-27T15:34:18.949234+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-27T15:34:18.946847+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# ResNet50 + BioViL-T distillation on NIH ChestX-ray14\n","\n","This standalone Kaggle workflow uses the fine-tuned **ResNet50 and BioViL-T as teachers**. A fresh ImageNet-initialized **ResNet50 is also the student**; it is not initialized from the teacher's fine-tuned checkpoint. Their validation-calibrated probability outputs are averaged with equal weights, then blended 50/50 with NIH hard labels. BioViL-T supplies training targets and is included in final comparisons; student inference uses ResNet50 alone.\n","\n","The notebook validates the official NIH patient split, pinned checkpoints, label/image ordering, and rebuilt teacher validation logits. BioViL-T uses its official image encoder and preprocessing (resize 512, center crop 448, grayscale replicated to RGB); ResNet50 uses its 384-pixel ImageNet-normalized training recipe and 0.1 drop path. Outputs are isolated under `/kaggle/working/distill/resnet50_biovil_t/`.\n","\n","## Kaggle prerequisites\n","\n","1. Attach NIH ChestX-ray14 and the **extracted** ResNet50 and BioViL-T single-model result bundles as Kaggle inputs. Each teacher run folder must contain its checkpoint, config, validation/test logits, calibration, and thresholds. Enable Internet for pretrained architecture initialization and enable a GPU.\n","2. Run the package setup cell without reinstalling Kaggle's CUDA-enabled PyTorch/torchvision.\n","3. Set `DATA_ROOT` to the NIH metadata and official lists directory if the default input path differs, then run the workflow cell. If teacher outputs have completed in the current Kaggle session before a later failure, set `RUN_ARGS = [\"--skip-teacher\"]` and rerun. Student optimizer state is not resumed.\n","\n","Checkpoint pins are ResNet50 `M08_RESNET50_ASL_384_CR` (`0a52192ad1c569e74865fd0c2e42cdb457826098129a9a183075c9c23d4d6625`) and BioViL-T `M11_BIOVIL_T_448_CR` (`0d067766186441e2163326a8c650081ba0aa7022705f27f1e677ddf09f17ddb3`). This is a separate experimental variant; it does not change the registered distillation protocol.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1553fe5b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.001397,"end_time":"2026-11-27T15:34:18.952372+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-27T15:34:18.950975+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Install notebook dependencies\n","\n","This leaves Kaggle's existing CUDA-enabled PyTorch and torchvision intact."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"a642a0ba","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-27T15:34:18.956678Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-27T15:34:18.956346Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-27T15:34:37.935475Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-27T15:34:37.934397Z"},"papermill":{"duration":18.983434,"end_time":"2026-11-27T15:34:37.937311+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-27T15:34:18.953877+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\u001b[31mERROR: pip's dependency resolver does not currently take into account all the packages that are installed. This behaviour is the source of the following dependency conflicts.\r\n","gradio-client 2.7.2 requires huggingface-hub<3.0,>=1.16.0, but you have huggingface-hub 0.36.2 which is incompatible.\r\n","gradio 6.30.0 requires huggingface-hub<3.0,>=1.16.0, but you have huggingface-hub 0.36.2 which is incompatible.\r\n","gradio 6.30.0 requires pillow<13.0,>=8.0, but you have pillow 13.0.0 which is incompatible.\r\n","diffusers 0.42.0 requires huggingface-hub<3.0,>=1.32.0, but you have huggingface-hub 0.36.2 which is incompatible.\u001b[0m\u001b[31m\r\n","\u001b[0mNote: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\n"]}],"source":["%pip install -q \"scikit-learn==1.6.1\" \"transformers==4.48.3\